      "problem": "Identify the surface $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+{z}^{2}=-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis and $a=b=2,\\,c=1.$",
