      "dom_id": "question-164543",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n4{y}^{2}-3{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.$",
